From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 07:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: display: mediatek: dsi: Add mediatek,vendor-link-timing

The Minimal Phone MP01's e-paper controller, an FPGA, decodes the MT6789
DSI link only with the horizontal blanking and D-PHY data lane timings
MediaTek's vendor driver programs; with the mainline ones it shows
garbled lines or a streaked picture. Describe that need on the DSI node.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/display/mediatek/mediatek,dsi.yaml | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/mediatek/mediatek,dsi.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/mediatek/mediatek,dsi.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/mediatek/mediatek,dsi.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/mediatek/mediatek,dsi.yaml
@@ -71,6 +71,13 @@
     items:
       - const: dphy
 
+  mediatek,vendor-link-timing:
+    type: boolean
+    description:
+      Program the horizontal blanking word counts and the D-PHY data lane
+      timings as MediaTek's vendor driver does, for a peripheral that only
+      decodes the link with those.
+
   port:
     $ref: '#/$defs/output-port'
     description:
-- 
2.47.0
